Fold (r173, PR #248, overdoingism): a new prompt-cache state buffer is faulted in with huge pages.
`server_prompt_cache::take()` reserves a buffer of 64 MiB or more, advises its 2 MiB-aligned part
`MADV_HUGEPAGE` and only then zero-fills it, so a multi-GiB slot state is faulted in 2 MiB pages
instead of 4 KiB ones (Linux, THP in `madvise` mode; `LLAMA_SERVER_CACHE_HUGEPAGE=0` restores 4 KiB
pages), and a recycled spare buffer keeps the pages it already has.  Measured on this box
(9950X3D/9950X3D2, `hugepage-bench` 3472 MiB): alloc+zero 470 -> 125 ms, and the server's prompt-cache
update for a 100K-token slot saving into a new 3.4 GiB buffer 828.1 -> 497.0 ms (-40 %); the
recycled-buffer case is unchanged (292.6 -> 291.0 ms).  Nothing is copied differently, so no text or
logit can move.  The submission's other half -- taking the batched state path above
`LLAMA_STATE_ASYNC_MAX_MIB` by cutting a piece at a byte offset -- is deliberately NOT taken: a cut
piece is not a window the meta backend accepts, so a 2-device `-sm tensor` 27B at `-c 266240` with a
250K-token slot aborts on the save (`GGML_ASSERT(size % chunk_size_full == 0)`,
ggml-backend-meta.cpp:2523) where the release path completes with identical logits; and on this box it
is not a win even single-device (324 MiB state: save 51.9 vs 32.0 ms, restore 53.9 vs 23.1 ms; 3.47 GiB
at 100K tokens: save 278 vs 304 ms, restore 281 vs 242 ms -- the pieces of a whole-slot state are large
enough that the per-tensor path already runs at 8-14 GiB/s).  See WORKLOG 261029.004.

r207 (2026-11-03): the host-pool-speed campaign is folded in here (it was developed as
wip/host-pool-speed/ and applies to this block's pool code).  Everything below is
`--host-experts pool` only; the default `pinned` mode is byte-for-byte unchanged.

  * A POOL-backed expert table is served by the device GATHER in the prefill band by default.
    Its whole-table staging is the slow path at every width (the source is the pageable model
    mapping plus the pool's host alias, and it degrades as coverage rises): 122B-A10B,
    -ncmoe 48, 5258-token prompt, -ub 2048, three R9700s -- pool FRAC 95 prefill
    1507.7-1631.3 t/s with the gather against pinned's 634-638, and 16.9 with the gather
    switched off; decode at parity (67.2-67.7).  Prefill logits are bit-identical to the
    staging path (KLD -0.000000 / same-top-p 100.000 %).  Mechanism: a new optional iface
    query moe_cache_pool_backed(backend, weight) (CUDA answers "this table's master is the
    read-only mapping"; the Meta backend forwards it to its simple devices) plus a BAND gate
    in sched_input_gatherable (n_tokens > moe_cache_band) -- taking the decode band over with
    the gather costs 1.2-4.1 t/s, because that band is served from the arena by the slot-remap
    read.  GGML_SCHED_DEVGATHER is three-valued: unset = pool-backed tables only (shipped),
    0 = kill switch, 1/force = the historical A/B arm (not the default: it costs a pinned
    master ~47 % prefill at two devices).  The gather resolves the arena first and the pool
    second, which subsumes MOE_HOST_POOL_COLD (COLD=0 19.57 vs 19.25-19.86 with COLD=1,
    15.54 without the gather).
  * MOE_HOST_POOL_RAM_PCT now SCALES EVERY TABLE instead of shaving the registration-order
    tail to the one-slot floor (122B at RAM_PCT=70: 26 of 144 tables at one slot, 10.94 t/s
    -> 17.44 t/s at identical pinned bytes, +73 % with SIZING=1; RAM_PCT=85 19.52 -> 20.97),
